# Plurals in Russian: коты, книги, окна
subtitle: "Make Russian nouns plural with three endings, ы, и and а, and meet они́ and мои́: э́то мои́ кни́ги, these are my books."
teaches: ["grammar/plurals"]
thumb: "band \"No s in Russian\" note \"кот → коты́\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Big and small in Russian: новый, новая, новое","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/12-russian-adjectives.cast"}

